  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Artisan.ORM 4.1.0\n\n- Bundled Roslyn mapper diagnostics ART001-ART007, including complete RequiredMethod.AllMain checks.\n- Added SqlParam factories mirroring typed Add*Param overloads, with nullable TVP omission, OUTPUT/RETURN support, and Roslyn checks for mapped TVP factories.\n- Fixed first-row reads, explicit projections, async cancellation, transaction ownership and cleanup.\n- Isolated mapper and procedure-parameter caches; preserved complete parameter metadata.\n- Corrected string and decimal normalization, dictionary parameter names, and enum auto-mapping.\n- Enforced finite negative-ID ranges and disposed MergeJoin enumerators.\n- Hardened optional DataReply status validation and exception messages.\n- Updated SqlClient and patched vulnerable transitive dependencies.\n- Updated sample SQL, articles, wiki, and the Claude Code skill. SQL changes require separate deployment.\n\nTargets: netstandard2.1, net8.0, net10.0. Includes XML documentation, SourceLink, and symbols.\nReadToLists supports two, three, or four result sets.\n\nCompatibility: excess decimal scale is rejected unless truncateFraction is true (truncation toward zero).\nExhausted negative-ID generators throw instead of wrapping. Undefined/composite DataReply statuses are rejected.\nMapper contract errors can now fail builds; see docs/analyzers.md and the changelog for migration guidance.\nNull short-ID TVP collections are now omitted consistently. Execute methods reuse one valid integer RETURN parameter; ambiguous or conflicting return parameters are rejected.\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/lobodava/artisan-orm/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
